<title>JAPAN: Japan to take appropriate steps on currencies--MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan to take appropriate steps on currencies--MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan will take appropriate steps against wild fluctuations in the currency market and considers excessive weakness or strength in the yen unfavourable, Finance Minister Hiroshi Mitsuzuka told a news conference on Friday.</p>
<p>He said Japan would take this stance in a meeting of finance ministers and central bankers of the Group of Seven (G7) nations on February 8.</p>
</text>
